From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ftgmac100: publish NC-SI data readiness through dormant

NC-SI requires the MAC carrier to stay on for its control packets, but this
also starts DHCP before sideband configuration finishes. The completion
callback currently only logs the actual NC-SI link result.

Keep the transport carrier and mark the interface dormant until NC-SI
reports a functional channel with link. Re-enter dormant on link loss,
stop or configuration failure, so networkd pauses/restarts dynamic address
acquisition on the real readiness transition without a MAC down/up.
The PHY-backed dedicated port is unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/faraday/ftgmac100.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/faraday/ftgmac100.c
@@ -1593,7 +1593,10 @@
 		phy_start(netdev->phydev);
 	}
 	if (priv->use_ncsi) {
-		/* If using NC-SI, set our carrier on and start the stack */
+		/* Keep the MAC carrier for NC-SI control packets, but withhold
+		 * operational readiness until the sideband channel is configured.
+		 */
+		netif_dormant_on(netdev);
 		netif_carrier_on(netdev);
 
 		/* Start the NCSI device */
@@ -1798,6 +1801,14 @@
 {
 	if (unlikely(nd->state != ncsi_dev_state_functional))
 		return;
+
+	/* Carrier must remain on so control requests can recover a lost link.
+	 * Dormant tells networkd/DHCP whether the data path is actually ready.
+	 */
+	if (nd->link_up)
+		netif_dormant_off(nd->dev);
+	else
+		netif_dormant_on(nd->dev);
 
 	netdev_dbg(nd->dev, "NCSI interface %s\n",
 		   nd->link_up ? "up" : "down");
